                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is funny as hell, very hard yet pretty enjoyable!\n\n+Visuals - okay graphics, sometimes you can't see enemies on the backgrounds because they are the same color, and the color palette is not super toxic as well, but it's okay. Pixel art is nice, and a naked guy with a huge censored sausage has funny animations.\n\n+Soundwork - okayish, ambient music tracks help not rage that much when you die over and over again.\n\n+Gameplay - Very cool game - it has its problems - nonremapable keys and unforgiving hit mechanics, yet it's very challenging and very enjoyable when you finally beat the level - 6 different levels - each has multiple stages and boss - each boss has multiple forms you have to beat, you have only 3 lives but every time you get damage you fly really high so count this as one life because once hit you will fly to the pit of doom or into another enemy/bullet. Yet after death you have pretty quick restart and completed stages are saved, even beaten boss forms are saved as well, so you don't have to play ALL over again once you die, that's cool.\n\n+Various naked guy skins - tan lines is the best one.\n+Steam achievements - Pretty hard to get all of them\n-At this moment steam overlay works but screenshots are not, no way to remap keys, music has only options to turn on/off no sliders to adjust volume.\n\nLong story short - this is a cool small game to waste a weekend, nice party game as well, very fun.",
